<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended flat on Wednesday after profit-taking emerged, prompted by highs for the fourth day in a row.</p>
<p>&quot;Prices were so high that people started to fear,&quot; a dealer in Madrid said. &quot;At these levels a little bit of profit-taking is pretty normal&quot;.</p>
<p>But every time the market dips people consider it a good buying opportunity and prices recover quickly, he said.</p>
<p>Chartists see a string of supports at 103.50, then 103.00 and 102.75 for Meff December 10-year bond futures.</p>
</text>
